From b15296c619aacf4433913cd2b89bce5bf02aec54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vaibhav <vgupta1192@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 06:47:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] Add a configure page to select/deselect the Adult
 catalog per install

manifest.js: createManifest(showAdult) replaces the static export,
building two variants with distinct manifest ids
(community.stremiojellyfin / .noadult) - Stremio has no concept of
reconfiguring an installed addon's catalog list in place, so this needs
to be two genuinely separate addons, not one that changes underneath an
existing install. behaviorHints.configurable added so Stremio shows a
reconfigure/gear option on either.

addon.js: wrapped the three resource handlers in buildInterface(showAdult)
and built both variants from it - no logic changes to the handlers
themselves, since the catalog handler was already driven purely by the
requested catalog id/type via CATALOG_LIBRARY_IDS, and Stremio only ever
requests a catalog id that's actually listed in whichever manifest it
fetched. The "no adult" variant's client simply never asks for
id: "adult" in the first place.

server.js: mounts both routers - the root path is unchanged from before
(full catalogs including Adult), so the existing install keeps working
exactly as it did; /hide-adult is the new variant, with its own
/hide-adult/manifest.json and /hide-adult/configure. Added a small
self-contained configure page (checkbox + Install button, no framework/
build step, matching the existing renderErrorPage's approach) at both
/configure (defaults checked) and /hide-adult/configure (defaults
unchecked, matching Stremio's own reconfigure flow which opens
<manifest-base>/configure for whichever variant is already installed).
The Install button builds the stremio:// URL client-side from the
checkbox state at click time.

Verified live: both manifests have the right (and only the right)
catalogs, both variants' Movies/Series catalogs work correctly, and the
existing root install's Adult catalog, stream resolution, and episode
lists are all unaffected.
